d a strong and enduring protection against a known evil being able to inflict harm on our society. Sarah Henderson You are a disgrace. Sue Lines Senator Birmingham, could you resume your seat. Murray Watt You're a disgrace. Sue Lines Senator Watt, order! Senator Henderson, please resume your seat. I will come back to you. Sarah Henderson President— Sue Lines I've asked you to resume your seat, Senator Henderson. Michaelia Cash Filthy grub. Sue Lines Senator Cash, I ask you to withdraw that remark. Michaelia Cash I withdraw. Sue Lines Thank you. Senator Henderson? Sarah Henderson President, Senator Watt said the most disgraceful thing. He is to withdraw it. I am disgusted in you. I'm so disgusted in you. Sue Lines Senator Henderson, I did not hear the remark, but in the interests of the Senate I ask Senator Watt to withdraw. Murray Watt Madam President, I withdraw. I referred to the text messages that Senator Henderson sent. That's what I said. I withdraw. Sue Lines Thank you. I think we just need to take a moment. I ask senators to listen to the debate abou","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10296","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2023-03-24/1"}
